WEBVTT

00:00:04.679 --> 00:00:12.730
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the fifth of October. Can you all hear me? Right, let's get through this before the floor gets too noisy.</v>

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:20.170
<v Callum Reid>Yep. There's a birthday cake in the office, by the way. Quite a serious bit of cake.</v>

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.329
<v Fiona Doyle>That's the most enthusiasm I've heard from you on a Monday.</v>

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:32.409
<v Callum Reid>And whose new car is that in the car park? Very shiny. Brave place to leave it.</v>

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.990
<v Tomasz Nowak>Not mine. Mine's mostly held together by the dirt.</v>

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:44.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Cake and depreciating assets covered. Anything already finished we need to separate out first?</v>

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:53.159
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I signed off the inspection on the turbine two water valve on Tuesday. That's done, not something still waiting on me.</v>

00:00:54.909 --> 00:00:59.460
<v Hannah Price>Ah, right. I remembered the inspection, couldn't remember whether the sign-off had happened.</v>

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:05.489
<v Grace Liu>And I already swapped the filter on the air dryer yesterday. That's finished as well.</v>

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.250
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, both closed. We're not putting either back in today's list.</v>

00:01:12.909 --> 00:01:18.859
<v Fiona Doyle>Just an observation from nights: noticed the palletiser was running a bit warm, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:20.829 --> 00:01:23.629
<v Callum Reid>Settled while they were still running, you mean?</v>

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.189
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah. Nothing outstanding from that, just passing on what was in the handover.</v>

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:35.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, context rather than another job. Right, onto what we are agreeing.</v>

00:01:38.099 --> 00:01:44.400
<v Sarah Okafor>Callum Reid, can you take vibration readings on the Water Booster Pump today at 2pm? That's fairly important.</v>

00:01:45.219 --> 00:01:48.719
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, um, readings only? We're not calling that a strip-down?</v>

00:01:50.689 --> 00:01:53.140
<v Sarah Okafor>Readings only. No strip-down in this one.</v>

00:01:55.290 --> 00:02:01.239
<v Callum Reid>Fine, I'll take the vibration readings on the Water Booster Pump today at 2pm. Fairly important, understood.</v>

00:02:02.599 --> 00:02:06.099
<v Tomasz Nowak>Look at that, asking before taking it apart. We're learning.</v>

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:09.500
<v Callum Reid>I knew you'd have something to say.</v>

00:02:10.719 --> 00:02:15.969
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz, can you inspect the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve for leaks on Friday? Low priority.</v>

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:23.090
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, I'll inspect the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve for leaks on Friday. Low priority, that's clear.</v>

00:02:24.039 --> 00:02:30.340
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, talking over you there. There's the purchase order side as well, isn't there? Separate from that inspection.</v>

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:39.650
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes. Han, can you chase the purchase order for the GT1 fuel valve this afternoon, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:02:40.439 --> 00:02:47.090
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll chase the purchase order for the GT1 fuel valve this afternoon if I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:52.650
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, so the purchase order chase isn't being bundled into the leak inspection.</v>

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.719
<v Hannah Price>No, separate things. Otherwise they end up looking like one enormous job.</v>

00:02:58.379 --> 00:03:05.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah, the other one for you: can you run a function test on the dryer on the 3rd? Low priority.</v>

00:03:07.669 --> 00:03:11.520
<v Hannah Price>On the 3rd, yeah? That's the date you've got against it?</v>

00:03:12.169 --> 00:03:16.020
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, on the 3rd. Keep that wording against it; low priority.</v>

00:03:18.189 --> 00:03:22.740
<v Hannah Price>Okay, agreed. I'll run a function test on the dryer on the 3rd.</v>

00:03:25.189 --> 00:03:28.340
<v Callum Reid>Was that me crackling, or did everyone get that?</v>

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:34.919
<v Hannah Price>I got a bit of robot voice, but the actual words came through.</v>

00:03:36.939 --> 00:03:39.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Teams doing its Monday thing. You're clear now.</v>

00:03:40.819 --> 00:03:50.969
<v Sarah Okafor>Callum Reid, can you go to the substation to pick up the replacement parts for the main isolation valve by the end of the week? Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:03:52.979 --> 00:04:01.030
<v Callum Reid>Yep, I'll go to the substation and pick up the replacement parts for the main isolation valve by the end of the week.</v>

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:05.960
<v Fiona Doyle>End of the week for the collection, then, not fitting them?</v>

00:04:06.789 --> 00:04:10.289
<v Callum Reid>That's what I've agreed, collection only. And fairly important, yeah.</v>

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:18.250
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good distinction. Picking up a box and fitting what's in it aren't quite the same duration.</v>

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:26.779
<v Priya Raman>While we're separating things out, I can't get to the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve until production gives us a window.</v>

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:32.050
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, there's no window confirmed. I can't tell you otherwise on this call.</v>

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:39.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. That stays blocked, then. We're not agreeing access or adding a job for today on that.</v>

00:04:42.199 --> 00:04:46.399
<v Priya Raman>Exactly. Just didn't want silence to sound like it was under way.</v>

00:04:48.449 --> 00:04:56.149
<v Priya Raman>What I can take is the guarding. I'll check the guarding on the IM3 tomorrow morning, and I'll make that top priority.</v>

00:04:57.459 --> 00:05:02.009
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Priya Raman. Tomorrow morning for the IM3 guarding check, top priority please.</v>

00:05:02.899 --> 00:05:06.050
<v Priya Raman>Yep, that's mine. Tomorrow morning, top of my list.</v>

00:05:07.199 --> 00:05:13.149
<v Grace Liu>Good. And just to be clear, agreeing a guarding check isn't us saying there's a confirmed defect.</v>

00:05:15.519 --> 00:05:19.720
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Let's not turn a check into a diagnosis before it's happened.</v>

00:05:21.129 --> 00:05:26.029
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace, can you investigate the pressure drop on the line 1 hydraulics by 11am?</v>

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:31.110
<v Grace Liu>Yes, I'll investigate the pressure drop on the line 1 hydraulics by 11am.</v>

00:05:31.529 --> 00:05:36.430
<v Tomasz Nowak>Pressure drop can cover a fair few things. Wouldn't jump straight to a component.</v>

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:41.319
<v Grace Liu>No, agreed. Investigation is what I'm taking, not promising a repair by 11am.</v>

00:05:42.649 --> 00:05:45.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Investigation by 11am is the agreement.</v>

00:05:46.629 --> 00:05:53.629
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, that all separates out properly. Finished work, blocked work, and the actual commitments. Less of a soup than usual.</v>

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:59.860
<v Sarah Okafor>That's the aim. Nothing else being added off the back of the observations.</v>

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:05.730
<v Priya Raman>And only about ten seconds of robot voice. Strong start to the week.</v>

00:06:07.529 --> 00:06:09.980
<v Callum Reid>We finished before the cake went, potentially.</v>

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:14.310
<v Grace Liu>You've got absolutely no evidence for that.</v>

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.769
<v Hannah Price>Quality can't support that claim either.</v>

00:06:18.569 --> 00:06:21.019
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, thanks, everyone. That's the stand-up done.</v>
